<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns A2 to LG-Caltex Oil's US CP programme.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns A2 to LG-Caltex Oil's US CP programme.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Monday that it had assigned its A2 short-term rating to LG-Caltex Oil Corp's $300 million U.S. commercial paper programme.</p>
<p>At the same time, S&amp;P has affirmed LG-Caltex's BBB+ long-term rating.</p>
<p>The ratings reflect the company's strong position in the South Korean oil-refining industry, support from its two share holders -- Caltex Petroleum Corp and the LG Group -- and high debt usage, S&amp;P said in a statement.</p>
<p>The outlook for the rating is stable, S&amp;P said.</p>
</text>
